<notes>
- The spec doesn't say what "in range" means for V9. I assumed an inclusive 0..100, set by the constants `RELIABILITY_MIN` and `RELIABILITY_MAX`. Please confirm the real bounds, or tell me which to change.
- V7 treats `max_units == capacity` as respected, and reports offending `wh` names in input order.
- V8 matches each expired `[sku, wh, qty]` against the entry's own `notified` list, one notification per expiry. Duplicate expiries therefore need duplicate notifications. Measured is the list of un-notified expiries across all entries. An entry with nothing expired passes, but an empty `entries` input fails.
- The tests are in `tests/test_validators_later.py`. I assumed the repo root is on the import path when they run.
</notes>
